## 7. CONCLUSION & KEY TAKEAWAYS
1. Dynamic SQL string formatting is inherently hazardous and must never be used.
2. Parameterized queries (Prepared Statements) provide mathematically complete defense against SQL injection.
3. Input validation acts as an essential secondary defense layer (defense-in-depth).
